erential/14068029/assets/12f33df5f036901c6069ee03a9ba8ccb05cde1071b7add3d1b310da12bb8298d.png) Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =1[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535586 true] [17592186157003 1145 "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWe are given the eigenvalue\n\n$$\n\\lambda_1 = 2\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding eigenvector $\\begin{bmatrix}1 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue\n\n$$\n\\lambda_2 = \\overline{\\lambda}_1\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v}_2 = \\overline{\\mathbf{v}}_1\n$$\n\nBut we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue\n\n$$\n\\lambda_1 = 2\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nand its associated eigenvector is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1}(t) &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}e^{2\\textrm{i}t} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ 1\\end{bm